<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette> a pk1:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Young et al. (1992) & Jaya et al. (2016) Emiliania huxleyi V/R calcite crystal coccolith rosette shield & interlocking spherical coccosphere mechanics (Emiliania huxleyi (Morphotypes A, B, B/C, C, R, O) & Gephyrocapsa / Calcidiscus / Coccolithus (Haptophyta))",
        "Young et al. (1992) & Jaya et al. (2016) Emiliania huxleyi V/R calcite crystal coccolith rosette shield & interlocking spherical coccosphere mechanics faithfully reproduces Emiliania huxleyi (Morphotypes A, B, B/C, C, R, O) & Gephyrocapsa / Calcidiscus / Coccolithus (Haptophyta) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette-6> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2022-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Emiliania huxleyi (Morphotypes A, B, B/C, C, R, O) & Gephyrocapsa / Calcidiscus / Coccolithus (Haptophyta) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 79.3/100, audit 2026-10-19-emiliania-calcite-rosette-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/models/2022-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette.py> ;
    schema:about "Emiliania huxleyi (Morphotypes A, B, B/C, C, R, O) & Gephyrocapsa / Calcidiscus / Coccolithus (Haptophyta)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Continuum fracture mechanics of calcite plates, measured interlock shear strength, independent vesicle rim tension data, detection of the SEM ellipse from pixels (centre, semi-axes and tilt are annotations), or verification of the Jaya 2016 / Walker 2018 venue-DOI pairs and the Reissner 1946 DOI (offline round)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: 3D V/R c-axis ring with exact orthogonality, T-shaped hammer-element rosette across morphotypes A/B/C/R and an acidification / CAP ablation control, 12-taxon L_d(N_seg) scaling table, spherical coccosphere Voronoi / Euler packing with a prescribed 2.36x buckling amplification, elliptical polar DoG spoke segmentation of the vendored SEM micrograph",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Pass 3: spherical-Voronoi suture network, reduced lumped-plate FE flat-punch nanoindentation with Coulomb + organic-interlock slide thresholds, plate bending fracture and cascade arrest tests, sigma_lock x overlap regime map; anisotropic vesicle rim tension law b/a = (2 + lambda)/(1 + 2 lambda) with an area-conserving contour relaxation and lambda* inferred from the SEM aspect ratio",
        "reported_in_source: Didymus et al. (1993): stage-specific E. huxleyi coccolith growth from proto-coccolith ring to T-shaped hammer elements of the distal shield",
        "reported_in_source: Jaya et al. (2016): E. huxleyi coccospheres confer mechanical protection; under nanoindentation individual coccoliths slide relative to each other and cracks are arrested at coccolith boundaries",
        "reported_in_source: Reissner (1946): point-load stiffness of a thin shallow spherical shell k = 4 E h^2 / (R sqrt(3 (1 - nu^2)))",
        "reported_in_source: Walker et al. (2018): the requirement for calcification differs between coccolithophore species; reduced calcification under acidification / CAP perturbation",
        "reported_in_source: Young et al. (1992): coccolith shield elements nucleate as alternating V- and R-units with mutually orthogonal calcite c-axis orientations on an organic baseplate ring; morphology follows from crystallographic control of {10-14} growth",
        "transfer_boundary: The 12-taxon 'observed' L_d column equals the formula prediction to the rounding digit, so r = 1.0000 is a self-consistency check, not a validation against measured taxa",
        "transfer_boundary: The contact model is a lumped network (one radial DOF per coccolith), not a continuum 3D FEM with Hertzian punch contact; E_cell, p_turgor, mu, sigma_lock, sigma_f, alpha_p, phi_res are order-of-magnitude `model_assumption` constants and no number is quoted from Jaya et al. (2016); the v2 2.36x amplification is not reproduced (model protection ratio ~1e4, measuring shedding rather than buckling)",
        "transfer_boundary: lambda* = 1.656 is a calibration to the hand-annotated SEM ellipse (92 x 78 px), not an independent measurement of vesicle rim tension anisotropy; only the normal Laplace balance is imposed" ;
    pk1:aristotelianEfficientCause "8. Crystal Accretion & TPMS" ;
    pk1:aristotelianMegistonGenos "IV. Protista & Monera" ;
    pk1:aristotelianPoionForm "Coiled Shells, Spicules & Gyroids" ;
    pk1:aristotelianPosonLaw "Raup (W,D,S) / Gyroid Mean H=0" ;
    pk1:aristotelianSubalternClass "Mineralized Protists (Silica/Calcite)" ;
    pk1:biologicalGenus "Emiliania" ;
    pk1:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/models/2022-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette.py; output: docs/media/emiliania_calcite_rosette_comparison.png; organism: Emiliania huxleyi (Morphotypes A, B, B/C, C, R, O) & Gephyrocapsa / Calcidiscus / Coccolithus (Haptophyta); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/9987db7d; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: 965ae13d1916a73bad9dca346e9176f4f9220e85b7c520cf8b7bb71057d4f791; artifact_sha256: a51c56828e0a56922fc52ef5383b841b1037b1b7d4aa33b14f593bf88059e97d; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/emiliania_calcite_rosette/emiliania_calcite_rosette_reference.json=6e0133f11f7fd993..., datasets/emiliania_calcite_rosette/emiliania_huxleyi_coccolith_specimen.jpg=94d4b431c4912727..., datasets/emiliania_calcite_rosette/scout_manifest.json=d838aa9cca83725c...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-emiliania-calcite-rosette-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Young et al. (1992): coccolith shield elements nucleate as alternating V- and R-units with mutually orthogonal calcite c-axis orientations on an organic baseplate ring; morphology follows from crystallographic control of {10-14} growth | Didymus et al. (1993): stage-specific E. huxleyi coccolith growth from proto-coccolith ring to T-shaped hammer elements of the distal shield | Jaya et al. (2016): E. huxleyi coccospheres confer mechanical protection; under nanoindentation individual coccoliths slide relative to each other and cracks are arrested at coccolith boundaries | Walker et al. (2018): the requirement for calcification differs between coccolithophore species; reduced calcification under acidification / CAP perturbation | Reissner (1946): point-load stiffness of a thin shallow spherical shell k = 4 E h^2 / (R sqrt(3 (1 - nu^2))); reconstructed_in_script: 3D V/R c-axis ring with exact orthogonality, T-shaped hammer-element rosette across morphotypes A/B/C/R and an acidification / CAP ablation control, 12-taxon L_d(N_seg) scaling table, spherical coccosphere Voronoi / Euler packing with a prescribed 2.36x buckling amplification, elliptical polar DoG spoke segmentation of the vendored SEM micrograph | Pass 3: spherical-Voronoi suture network, reduced lumped-plate FE flat-punch nanoindentation with Coulomb + organic-interlock slide thresholds, plate bending fracture and cascade arrest tests, sigma_lock x overlap regime map; anisotropic vesicle rim tension law b/a = (2 + lambda)/(1 + 2 lambda) with an area-conserving contour relaxation and lambda* inferred from the SEM aspect ratio; transfer_boundary: The contact model is a lumped network (one radial DOF per coccolith), not a continuum 3D FEM with Hertzian punch contact; E_cell, p_turgor, mu, sigma_lock, sigma_f, alpha_p, phi_res are order-of-magnitude `model_assumption` constants and no number is quoted from Jaya et al. (2016); the v2 2.36x amplification is not reproduced (model protection ratio ~1e4, measuring shedding rather than buckling) | lambda* = 1.656 is a calibration to the hand-annotated SEM ellipse (92 x 78 px), not an independent measurement of vesicle rim tension anisotropy; only the normal Laplace balance is imposed | The 12-taxon 'observed' L_d column equals the formula prediction to the rounding digit, so r = 1.0000 is a self-consistency check, not a validation against measured taxa; does_not_claim: Continuum fracture mechanics of calcite plates, measured interlock shear strength, independent vesicle rim tension data, detection of the SEM ellipse from pixels (centre, semi-axes and tilt are annotations), or verification of the Jaya 2016 / Walker 2018 venue-DOI pairs and the Reissner 1946 DOI (offline round)]" ;
    pk1:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1002/sapm194625180>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/356516a0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/ncomms11904>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-018-04168-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.1993.0073> ;
    pk1:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette-model-fidelity>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette-morphometric-validation>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette-overall>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette-parameter-expressivity>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette-repro-package>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette-source-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette-specimen-match> ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-emiliania-calcite-rosette-audit-v3-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-emiliania-calcite-rosette-audit-v3-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette-10>,
