<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette-code-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Young et al. (1992) & Jaya et al. (2016) Emiliania huxleyi V/R calcite crystal coccolith rosette shield & interlocking spherical coccosphere mechanics — Code-to-model traceability: 85/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The module header lists the Pass 3 sections and their limits, the contact-model docstring maps every stiffness and threshold to its formula (k_cell, k_mem via Reissner 1946, k_ij lap joint, N_ij hoop force, alpha_p P/h^2 fracture), the vesicle functions cite the support-function derivation, the Panel E title now says \"prescribed\", and the new Lean theorems are named in the measurement sources. Deductions: the vendored JSON governing equation for the T-head uses tanh while the code is linear in max(Omega - 1, 0) — a formula mismatch between the stated source and the implementation (-5); the shaft-width factor 0.62 w_0, the morphotype-R factors 1.28 / 1.45, the 0.28 angular-pitch factor, the acidification spoke factor 0.55 + 0.35 Omega and the interlock threshold 1.35 are uncited (-5); the 0.042 / 0.012 / 2.36 buckling constants are labelled prescribed but not traced to any derivation (-3); the 44.61 deg constant is documented but dead (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "datasets/emiliania_calcite_rosette/emiliania_calcite_rosette_reference.json L75–L75: t_head_hammer_width governing equation uses tanh(max(Omega-1, 0)) whereas the code uses a linear slope <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/datasets/emiliania_calcite_rosette/emiliania_calcite_rosette_reference.json#L75-L75>",
        "models/2022-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette.py L264–L298: Uncited constants: 0.225 slope (L264), 0.55 + 0.35 Omega (L267), 0.62 and 1.28 (L272), interlock threshold 1.35 (L278), 0.28 and 1.45 (L298) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/models/2022-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette.py#L264-L298>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette-code-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette-code-traceability-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.5e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette-model-fidelity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Young et al. (1992) & Jaya et al. (2016) Emiliania huxleyi V/R calcite crystal coccolith rosette shield & interlocking spherical coccosphere mechanics — Model fidelity to source: 80/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The V/R ring, T-head rosette and Euler packing are implemented as before, and the two Pass 3 mechanisms are mechanically coherent: the contact model couples a Reissner shell stiffness, a protoplast foundation and lap-joint suture springs on the actual spherical Voronoi edges, resolves slide / fracture / arrest / exposure cascades, and reproduces the Jaya et al. (2016) qualitative order (sliding at 13.2 uN before apex fracture at 55.1 uN = sigma_f h^2 / alpha_p, arrested with sigma_neigh/sigma_f = 0.28); the vesicle law b/a = (2 + lambda)/(1 + 2 lambda) is the exact support-function solution of tau(psi) kappa(psi) = p and the relaxation reproduces it to 0.0034 over lambda in [1, 2.5]. Deductions: the coccosphere buckling load 0.042 E h^2 (1 + 0.012 (N - 12)) and the 2.36x amplification remain prescribed, unsourced constants that the new contact model does not reproduce (-6); the T-head slope 0.225 is tuned so that Omega = 4.2 gives the JSON's 1.72 and is linear whereas the vendored governing equation uses tanh(max(Omega - 1, 0)) (-4); the contact model is lumped (one radial DOF per plate, no Hertzian contact, no plate bending field) with all seven constants `model_assumption` (-4); the vesicle model imposes only the normal Laplace balance, with tangential equilibrium assumed to be supplied by anchored cytoskeleton, and lambda* is a fit (-3); the 44.61 deg rhombohedral angle is stated but unused and the 22.5 / 1.05 volume ratios are hard-coded (-3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "models/2022-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette.py L200–L202: Rhombohedral {10-14} angle 44.61 deg stated but unused; R/V volume ratios 22.5 / 1.05 hard-coded without source <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/models/2022-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette.py#L200-L202>",
        "models/2022-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette.py L264–L264: t_head_ratio = 1 + 0.225 c_CAP max(Omega-1, 0): linear slope tuned to give 1.72 at Omega = 4.2; JSON governing equation (line 75) uses tanh <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/models/2022-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette.py#L264-L264>",
        "models/2022-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette.py L470–L478: Prescribed 0.042 E h^2 (1 + 0.012 (N-12)) buckling load and interlock_amplification = 2.36 with no source; not reproduced by the contact model <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/models/2022-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette.py#L470-L478>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette-model-fidelity-4> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette-morphometric-validation> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Young et al. (1992) & Jaya et al. (2016) Emiliania huxleyi V/R calcite crystal coccolith rosette shield & interlocking spherical coccosphere mechanics — Morphometric validation: 74/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "measure_morphoeval() now returns 16 measurements with reference values, including seven new ones: Voronoi edge count 42 vs 3(F-2), arrest ratio 0.28 (< 1), capacity ratio Pi = 0.286 (< 1, sliding first), relaxed b/a 0.8461 vs 0.8478, lambda* 1.6562 vs the naive (a/b)^3 estimate 1.6411, ellipse RMS residual 0.198 % vs 1.087 % pixel precision, and the protection ratio ~1.04e4 vs 2.36 reported as a negative control. Deductions: the headline 12-taxon correlation r = 1.0000 / RMSE 0.004 um compares an \"observed\" column that equals the formula to the rounding digit — a circular validation that v2 credited (-10); the arrest and capacity references (1.0) are decision thresholds and the 2.36 reference is the unsourced v2 constant, so three of the seven new measurements have no literature anchor (-6); the specimen b/a and L_d measurements are transcriptions of annotations, and the vesicle b/a comparison is against the same annotation (-6); no measured nanoindentation force, stiffness or fracture load from Jaya et al. (2016) is compared because the paper could not be re-read offline (-4)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "datasets/emiliania_calcite_rosette/emiliania_calcite_rosette_reference.json L96–L107: cross_taxa_coccolithophore_table: l_d_obs_um = round(l_d_pred_um, 2) for every row <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/datasets/emiliania_calcite_rosette/emiliania_calcite_rosette_reference.json#L96-L107>",
        "models/2022-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette.py L1661–L1669: Protection-ratio measurement anchored to the unsourced v2 2.36 constant; explicitly reported as not reproduced (~1e4, dominated by assumed E_cell) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/models/2022-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette.py#L1661-L1669>",
        "models/2022-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette.py L374–L426: evaluate_cross_taxa_scaling: r = 1.0000 against l_d_obs_um values that equal l_d_pred_um to the rounding digit for all 12 taxa (circular) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/models/2022-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette.py#L374-L426>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette-measurement-12-taxon-coccolithophore-proto-coccolith-linear-scaling-correlation-l-d-n-seg>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette-measurement-cell-exposure-load-protection-ratio-f-expose-interlocked-f-expose-truncated-t-heads-negative-control>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette-measurement-emiliania-huxleyi-sem-specimen-calibrated-distal-shield-major-length-l-d-emiliania-huxleyi-coccolith-specimen-jpg>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette-measurement-emiliania-huxleyi-sem-specimen-coccolith-elliptical-aspect-ratio-b-a-emiliania-huxleyi-coccolith-specimen-jpg>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette-measurement-emiliania-huxleyi-sem-specimen-segmented-radial-spoke-count-n-seg-emiliania-huxleyi-coccolith-specimen-jpg>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette-measurement-interlock-shear-capacity-over-apex-plate-bending-capacity-pi-sliding-first-if-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette-measurement-interlocked-coccosphere-nanoindentation-neighbour-bending-stress-ratio-sigma-neigh-sigma-f-at-first-apex-fracture-arrest-criterion-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette-measurement-morphotype-a-canonical-distal-shield-major-length-l-d-n-seg-32>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette-measurement-morphotype-a-cap-polysaccharide-t-shaped-hammer-head-expansion-ratio-w-head-w-shaft>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette-measurement-ocean-acidification-cap-polysaccharide-ablation-negative-control-t-head-ratio-omega-0-75>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette-measurement-relaxed-vesicle-rim-contour-aspect-ratio-b-a-at-inferred-tension-anisotropy-lambda-vs-sem-baseplate-fit>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette-measurement-relaxed-vesicle-rim-deviation-from-best-fit-ellipse-rms-radial-residual-of-a-vs-sem-one-pixel-fit-precision>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette-measurement-spherical-coccosphere-euler-polyhedral-characteristic-chi-v-e-f-n-cocc-16>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette-measurement-spherical-voronoi-coccosphere-suture-edge-count-e-f-16-tiles-vs-euler-trivalent-3-f-2>,
