<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette-overall> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Young et al. (1992) & Jaya et al. (2016) Emiliania huxleyi V/R calcite crystal coccolith rosette shield & interlocking spherical coccosphere mechanics — MorphoEval overall 79.3/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 3 closes both v2 remediation items with honest reduced models: a Voronoi suture-network nanoindentation contact model that reproduces the Jaya et al. (2016) qualitative sequence (suture sliding first, apex fracture arrested at the neighbours, punch-through exposure later) and a tension-anisotropy law for the Golgi vesicle rim that yields the SEM baseplate aspect ratio at an inferred lambda*, both with provenance-tagged constants, two new Lean theorems, seven new measurements and four new self-test checks. The re-read, however, finds that several v2 strengths were over-credited: the 12-taxon scaling validation is circular, the specimen aspect ratio and distal length are transcriptions of hand annotations (only the spoke count is detected), the buckling amplification and T-head slope are prescribed or tuned, the vendored governing equation (tanh) disagrees with the code (linear), the new JSON is not SHA-pinned, the regime map ignores `--n-cocc`, and two venue/DOI pairs are inconsistent. Overall 79.3 (down from 91.8). Overall 79.3/100 (faithfulness 76.4, reproducibility 86.0); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 9987db7d; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 80, Morphological realism / specimen match 72, Parameter expressivity 84, Morphometric validation 74, Source and data traceability 82, Code-to-model traceability 85, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/emiliania_calcite_rosette_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2022-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette.py at 9987db7d, image/png, 962700 B, 2371×2099 px, artifact_sha256 a51c56828e0a56922fc52ef5383b841b1037b1b7d4aa33b14f593bf88059e97d (sha256 a51c56828e0a56922fc52ef5383b841b1037b1b7d4aa33b14f593bf88059e97d), spec_fingerprint 965ae13d1916a73bad9dca346e9176f4f9220e85b7c520cf8b7bb71057d4f791. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 965ae13d1916a73bad9dca346e9176f4f9220e85b7c520cf8b7bb71057d4f791; artifact_sha256: a51c56828e0a56922fc52ef5383b841b1037b1b7d4aa33b14f593bf88059e97d; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/emiliania_calcite_rosette/emiliania_calcite_rosette_reference.json=6e0133f11f7fd993..., datasets/emiliania_calcite_rosette/emiliania_huxleyi_coccolith_specimen.jpg=94d4b431c4912727..., datasets/emiliania_calcite_rosette/scout_manifest.json=d838aa9cca83725c...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-emiliania-calcite-rosette-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Young et al. (1992): coccolith shield elements nucleate as alternating V- and R-units with mutually orthogonal calcite c-axis orientations on an organic baseplate ring; morphology follows from crystallographic control of {10-14} growth | Didymus et al. (1993): stage-specific E. huxleyi coccolith growth from proto-coccolith ring to T-shaped hammer elements of the distal shield | Jaya et al. (2016): E. huxleyi coccospheres confer mechanical protection; under nanoindentation individual coccoliths slide relative to each other and cracks are arrested at coccolith boundaries | Walker et al. (2018): the requirement for calcification differs between coccolithophore species; reduced calcification under acidification / CAP perturbation | Reissner (1946): point-load stiffness of a thin shallow spherical shell k = 4 E h^2 / (R sqrt(3 (1 - nu^2))); reconstructed_in_script: 3D V/R c-axis ring with exact orthogonality, T-shaped hammer-element rosette across morphotypes A/B/C/R and an acidification / CAP ablation control, 12-taxon L_d(N_seg) scaling table, spherical coccosphere Voronoi / Euler packing with a prescribed 2.36x buckling amplification, elliptical polar DoG spoke segmentation of the vendored SEM micrograph | Pass 3: spherical-Voronoi suture network, reduced lumped-plate FE flat-punch nanoindentation with Coulomb + organic-interlock slide thresholds, plate bending fracture and cascade arrest tests, sigma_lock x overlap regime map; anisotropic vesicle rim tension law b/a = (2 + lambda)/(1 + 2 lambda) with an area-conserving contour relaxation and lambda* inferred from the SEM aspect ratio; transfer_boundary: The contact model is a lumped network (one radial DOF per coccolith), not a continuum 3D FEM with Hertzian punch contact; E_cell, p_turgor, mu, sigma_lock, sigma_f, alpha_p, phi_res are order-of-magnitude `model_assumption` constants and no number is quoted from Jaya et al. (2016); the v2 2.36x amplification is not reproduced (model protection ratio ~1e4, measuring shedding rather than buckling) | lambda* = 1.656 is a calibration to the hand-annotated SEM ellipse (92 x 78 px), not an independent measurement of vesicle rim tension anisotropy; only the normal Laplace balance is imposed | The 12-taxon 'observed' L_d column equals the formula prediction to the rounding digit, so r = 1.0000 is a self-consistency check, not a validation against measured taxa; does_not_claim: Continuum fracture mechanics of calcite plates, measured interlock shear strength, independent vesicle rim tension data, detection of the SEM ellipse from pixels (centre, semi-axes and tilt are annotations), or verification of the Jaya 2016 / Walker 2018 venue-DOI pairs and the Reissner 1946 DOI (offline round)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: models/2022-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette.py:120-146 — the Pass 3 JSON coccosphere_contact_vesicle_tension_reference.json is loaded (L522-526) but not SHA-256 pinned in EXPECTED_SHA256 / verify_dataset_integrity. Add it to the pinned set and to the reference-JSON specimen metadata so the Pass 3 constants are integrity-checked.",
        "remediation needed: models/2022-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette.py:1476-1539 — render_growth_gif is unchanged from Pass 2; add the vesicle rim relaxation (lambda from 1 to lambda*) as a third GIF panel or frames so the Pass 3 eccentricity mechanism is animated alongside the rosette growth.",
        "remediation needed: models/2022-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette.py:264 vs datasets/emiliania_calcite_rosette/emiliania_calcite_rosette_reference.json:75 — the code's linear t_head_ratio = 1 + 0.225 c_CAP max(Omega - 1, 0) (slope tuned to give 1.72 at Omega = 4.2) does not match the vendored governing equation tanh(max(Omega - 1, 0)). Make the JSON and the code agree and derive or cite the slope / saturation.",
        "remediation needed: models/2022-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette.py:31-46 and datasets/emiliania_calcite_rosette/paper_citations.bib — Jaya et al. (2016) venue \"Nat. Commun. / J. Struct. Biol.\" and Walker et al. (2018) \"Nat. Commun. / New Phytol.\" with DOI 10.1038/s41467-018-04168-9 are internally inconsistent (the Walker title is a New Phytologist paper); the seed-paper DOI is 10.1038/356145a0 in the campaign record vs 10.1038/356516a0 here. Resolve all three online in Pass 4 and update header, bib and audit references.",
        "remediation needed: models/2022-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette.py:374-426 with datasets/emiliania_calcite_rosette/emiliania_calcite_rosette_reference.json:96-107 — l_d_obs_um equals round(l_d_pred_um, 2) for all 12 taxa, so r = 1.0000 / RMSE 0.004 um is circular. Replace the observed column with per-taxon literature measurements (with citations) or relabel Panel C and measurement #8 as a self-consistency check and drop the correlation from the validation set.",
        "remediation needed: models/2022-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette.py:470-478 and 1287 — the coccosphere buckling load 0.042 E h^2 (1 + 0.012 (N - 12)) and interlock_amplification = 2.36 are prescribed constants with no source, and the Pass 3 contact model yields a protection ratio ~1e4 for a different quantity (shedding, not buckling). Either derive the buckling load from the Reissner / Zoelly shell formula already used in the contact model and compute the interlock amplification from the suture stiffness, or remove the 2.36x claim from Panels D/E and measurement #4.",
        "remediation needed: models/2022-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette.py:578-806 — the contact model is a lumped network (one radial DOF per coccolith) with seven order-of-magnitude constants; a Pass 4 step toward the v2 item is a per-coccolith Kirchhoff plate bending field (or at least a Hertzian punch contact on the apex tile) and at least one force / stiffness anchor read from Jaya et al. (2016) once the paper can be accessed.",
        "remediation needed: models/2022-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette.py:818 — evaluate_contact_regime_map builds the default N_cocc = 16 tiling and ignores the --n-cocc override that Panel G and the measurements honour; thread n_cocc through, and expose sigma_lock, E_cell, p_turgor and lambda as CLI overrides (L1917-1924).",
        "remediation needed: models/2022-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette.py:994-1078 (L1013) — the SEM ellipse centre, semi-axes (92 x 78 px), tilt and calibration are JSON annotations; b/a = 0.8478, L_d = 3.50 um and the Pass 3 lambda* all rest on them. Fit the ellipse from pixels (e.g. edge points of the distal shield rim, least-squares conic) and report the fitted vs annotated values with a residual." ;
    pk1:hasScore 7.93e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette-parameter-expressivity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Young et al. (1992) & Jaya et al. (2016) Emiliania huxleyi V/R calcite crystal coccolith rosette shield & interlocking spherical coccosphere mechanics — Parameter expressivity: 84/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 3 adds genuine sweeps whose outcomes change qualitatively: the sigma_lock in {5..400 MPa} x t_head_ratio in [1, 2] regime map moves through shedding -> interlock sliding -> sliding-then-arrested fracture, with fracture-first only at sigma_lock >= 200 MPa and crack propagation only at 400 MPa and ratio 2.0; the F_expose vs overlap sweep is monotone; the vesicle law is swept over lambda in [1, 2.5] and inverted on the 12-taxon b/a column (lambda 1.08-1.69). The Pass 2 morphotype / acidification regimes, Omega and N_cocc sweeps and the seven CLI overrides remain. Deductions: evaluate_contact_regime_map always builds the N_cocc = 16 tiling and ignores `--n-cocc` (only Panel G and the measurements honour the override) (-6); sigma_lock, E_cell, p_turgor, lambda and the load ramp have no CLI exposure (-5); the t_head_ratio axis of the regime map is entered directly rather than driven through Omega / c_CAP, so the CAP-acidification link is not swept end to end (-3); Panel D's 2.36x N_cocc sweep still reports a prescribed constant (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "models/2022-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette.py L818–L818: til = build_coccosphere_voronoi_tiling() — regime map not wired to the n_cocc override <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/models/2022-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette.py#L818-L818>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette-parameter-expressivity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette-parameter-expressivity-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.4e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette-repro-package> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Young et al. (1992) & Jaya et al. (2016) Emiliania huxleyi V/R calcite crystal coccolith rosette shield & interlocking spherical coccosphere mechanics — Reproducibility package: 90/100" ;
